+# Roadmap
+
+## Terms
+
+- The program is `phial`.
+- The host runs the program.
+- The guest is the virtual machine that the host runs.
+- Env mode describes a secret that the guest reads from a file.
+- Proxy mode describes a secret that the host injects into an outbound request.
+- A grant is a time box on one secret.
+
+## Threat model
+
+- The host is trusted, and the guest is not.
+- Only the host user adds a provider, removes a provider, or grants access.
+- The guest agent cannot add a provider. It may only use what the host already granted.
+- Leave room for a future request path, where the guest agent asks the host for a grant and the host answers.
+- One grant covers one SSH key, one GnuPG key, one API key, or one other secret.
+- Revocation at the provider is out of scope. Removing the local file is not revocation at the provider.
+
+## Host matrix
+
+- The host runs Fedora Workstation 45 during development.
+- The host takes QEMU and waypipe from DNF for now.
+- At the target, the host runs GNOME OS and takes the user space tools from Homebrew.
+- The guest runs Fedora Workstation 45.
+- The guest installs from a kickstart and boots with UEFI and Secure Boot.
+
+## Host toolchain
+
+- Install the user space tools with Homebrew, so one manifest works on both hosts.
+- Homebrew covers virtiofsd, passt, Caddy, socat, GnuPG, swtpm, FreeRDP, wl-clipboard, and zenity.
+- Take QEMU and waypipe from DNF on the development host.
+- Make sure that Fedora builds QEMU with virglrenderer.
+- Fedora also ships a GNOME pinentry and KeePassXC.
+- Record a note for each tool that Homebrew does not provide on Linux.
+- Keep the KeePassXC window open and unlocked, so its Secret Service answers one `keepassxc://` lookup with no prompt.
+
+## Historical notes
+
+- [QEMU and VM arguments](https://gist.github.com/pojntfx/b860e123e649504bcd298aa6e92c4043) holds the raw QEMU flags from earlier work.
+- [Headless virgl and waypipe](https://gist.github.com/pojntfx/32e13d3eda90f34a56913e9fb53e7ac3) holds the vsock and waypipe flow from earlier work.
+- Read both before you change the launcher or the display path.
+
+## Host acceptance
+
+- Run `qemu-system-x86_64 -display help`, and make sure that it lists `egl-headless`.
+- Run `qemu-system-x86_64 -device virtio-vga-gl,help`, and make sure that it lists `venus` and `drm_native_context`.
+- Run `qemu-system-x86_64 -device help`, and make sure that it lists `qemu-xhci`, `vhost-vsock-pci`, `vhost-user-fs-pci`, and `virtio-blk-pci`.
+- Run `qemu-system-x86_64 -machine q35,help`, and make sure that it lists `smm` and `kernel-irqchip`.
+- Run `virtiofsd --version`, and make sure that it reports the Rust backend.
+- Run `virt-fw-vars --help`, and make sure that it lists a DER enrollment flag.
+

